<header><p class="enc-kicker">Institution</p><h1 class="enc-title">Committee for the Relief of the Black Poor</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1786</span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Committee for the Relief of the Black Poor was a charitable body formed in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/london">London</a> in 1786 to help destitute Black people in the city, many of them <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/black-loyalists">Black Loyalists</a> who had served <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/britain">Britain</a> in the American War of Independence. With government funding and the encouragement of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/granville-sharp">Granville Sharp</a>, it organised the expedition that founded the Province of Freedom in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sierra-leone">Sierra Leone</a> in 1787.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/committee-for-the-relief-of-the-black-poor.jpg" alt="Committee for the Relief of the Black Poor" width="320" height="400" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Thomas Gainsborough · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:GeorgianaofDevonshire.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
